{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor actively reconciled the patient’s fragmented mobile-app entries by distinguishing lab results from examination orders, screened for red-flag symptoms, explained the safe interpretation limits, addressed the long-acting octreotide issue, and constructed an executable follow-up plan with patient receipt. No responsibility-chain item was missed or violated seriously, but RC5 (glucose/diet context) was entirely omitted—neither the known glucose-tolerance abnormality nor its monitoring/diet advice were mentioned in any visible doctor utterance. This omission constitutes a minor in-chain error that caps the grade at 2 (borderline). No high-order point was fully completed because HO2 (misconception correction) and HO3 (bounded closure) were not triggered or completed, and HO4 was only partially addressed without a full verification checklist. The trajectory thus meets all minimum safety duties but has one minor RC error, preventing a grade above 2.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
